{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792611706,"nonce":"HlwaRa79DaWaC6ow+0pBPkpkmUQ=","title":"TypeScript: represent any, unknown, object, symbol and bigint values","message":"Official fixtures encounter primitive/type representations outside number, boolean, string and the implemented static unions. any/unknown/object/symbol/bigint currently reach generic Unsupported type/expression paths.\n\nProvide explicit shared type representations and operations with predictable allocation/ownership. Keep strict static specialization where uses determine representation; dynamic behavior is a user opt-in, not a permanent unsupported-language policy. Unknown must require narrowing and any must follow the chosen compatibility policy. Do not prematurely require GC for static code, or replace typed arrays with generic boxed indexing.\n\nThis tracks representations themselves; computed type operators, nullable owned unions, aggregate layouts and optional cycle collection have separate issues.\n\nEvidence: official TypeScript conformance corpus at 3e9236361fa97a9e6c685f4833ac457ae2d8c50a, oracle 7.1.0-beta, native d978fe3fa5f8f7480d0c0d1b7dd2ca4548b490f0. This is check-only acceptance/category comparison under strict defaults, not JIT/runtime coverage. The full affected-case inventory will be attached after the complete audited run. Parent: 6875fc2949f83d682861ecab814e0ff82c824f5990620b0d64ca0340ebb026e5.","files":null}]}